'''Moota Engatoo''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[merchant]] who was active during the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Trivia">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/twin-suns-trivia-gallery|text="Twin Suns" Trivia Gallery}} {{C|image 4 of 6}}</ref> In the [[Standard year|year]] [[2 BBY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of "[[Twin Suns (episode)|Twin Suns]]" to [[2 BBY]].</ref> he was present at a remote outpost on the [[desert]] [[planet]] of [[Tatooine]]; and there he told young [[Padawan]] [[Ezra Bridger]] some information on where to go next in his [[Mission to Tatooine (Imperial Era)|search]] for [[Maul]],<ref name="Trivia" /> the former [[Sith Lord]] who intended to [[Death|kill]] [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]].<ref name="Twin Suns">{{Rebels|Twin Suns (episode)}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The character Moota Engatoo was intended to appear in "[[Twin Suns (episode)|Twin Suns]],"<ref name="Trivia" /> the twentieth episode of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki> [[Star Wars Rebels Season Three|third season]].<ref name="Twin Suns Episode">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/twin-suns-episode-guide|text="Twin Suns" Episode Guide &#124; Star Wars Rebels}}</ref> Engatoo was fully designed prior to being cut from the episode<ref name="Trivia" /> due to time constraints.<ref name="Rebels Recon">{{SWYouTube|8eIZsJsck7A|Rebels Recon #3.20: Inside "Twin Suns" &#124; Star Wars Rebels|sw_url=video/rebels-recon-inside-twin-suns}}</ref> In the early drafts of the episode, Ezra Bridger was supposed to go to Tatooine along with his master [[Kanan Jarrus]] and follow a path of clues left by Maul,<ref name="Trivia 2">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/twin-suns-trivia-gallery|text="Twin Suns" Trivia Gallery}} {{C|image 3 of 6}}</ref> including a visit to a remote outpost where Engatoo would give Bridger some information that would lead to Maul.<ref name="Trivia" /> The idea of Jarrus' involvement was ultimately abandoned<ref name="Rebels Recon" /> and Bridger was guided by the [[holocron]] fragments instead of clues.<ref name="Twin Suns" /><ref name="Trivia 2" />

